{
  "slug": "music-catalog-diligence",
  "name": "Music Catalog Diligence",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Music Catalog Diligence helps catalog buyers, sellers, and financing teams review music catalog deals faster and with better evidence. It turns messy data rooms into source-cited workpapers by normalizing royalty statements, checking rights and metadata gaps, analyzing NPS/NLS, flagging diligence risks, and preparing buyer, seller, or lender-ready deal packages.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **9 skills**, **5 agents**, **6 commands** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (9): `catalog-analysis` (Use when analyzing or valuing a music catalog for acquisition, financing, sale, or investment diligence), `catalog-ingest` (Use when ingesting a music catalog data room, royalty statements, rights files, metadata exports, or messy catalog spreadsheets…), `diligence-kickoff` (Use when starting a new music catalog deal, setting up a data room review, creating a deal workspace,…), `financing-underwrite` (Use when underwriting a music catalog for an advance, loan, credit facility, securitization, collateral package, or royalty-backed financing), `ic-memo-package` (Use when creating an investment committee memo, buyer diligence package, bid recommendation, seller cleanup report, financing pack, or…), `post-close-admin` (Use after a music catalog acquisition closes, when transferring royalty administration, updating registrations, tracking ownership changes, monitoring first…), `rights-diligence` (Use when reviewing music catalog ownership, chain of title, split sheets, publishing agreements, recording agreements, assignments, sample clearances,…), `royalty-audit` (Use when auditing music royalty statements, checking reported revenue, normalizing royalty ledgers, finding missing income, validating NPS/NLS, reviewing…), and 1 more\n- **Agents** (5): `diligence-qc-reviewer` (Performs final quality control on a music catalog diligence package before it is shared with an IC, buyer,…), `metadata-reconciler` (Reconciles music catalog metadata across track lists, royalty statements, registrations, identifiers, and analytics exports), `rights-chain-reviewer` (Reviews music catalog chain of title, ownership support, split sheets, assignments, samples, reversions, territory limits, and transferability), `royalty-audit-analyst` (Audits normalized music royalty ledgers and royalty workpapers for completeness, gross-to-net issues, duplicate imports, timing errors, PRO/MLC anomalies,…), `valuation-sensitivity-analyst` (Reviews music catalog valuation assumptions, NPS/NLS bridges, concentration, decay, recoupment, reserves, and downside/base/upside scenarios)\n- **Commands** (6): `catalog-analyze` (Analyze normalized music catalog royalties, risk, concentration, and valuation scenarios), `catalog-diligence` (Run the end-to-end music catalog diligence workflow from workspace setup through package readiness), `catalog-ingest` (Normalize a catalog data room into auditable catalog, royalty, rights, and evidence artifacts), `catalog-kickoff` (Set up a music catalog deal workspace and first diligence request list), `catalog-package` (Assemble an IC memo, seller cleanup report, financing pack, or post-close administration package), `catalog-qc` (Run diligence quality control before a catalog package is shared)\n- **Hooks** (2): `PreToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install music-catalog-diligence@claude-community` from `recoupable/music-catalog-diligence`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
